78. FINAL CANONICAL PRINCIPLE
==================================================

"PRSL-AI does not grant authority merely because an identity is
known. Every meaningful access operation is evaluated through
explicit authorization, defined scope, applicable privacy and
security policies, and governance constraints."

==================================================
79. FINAL STATEMENT
==================================================

Permissions are the controlled boundary between intelligence
and authority.

@iriel may understand what the user wants.

The Router may understand which capability can perform it.

The Device may possess the technical capability.

But none of these facts alone authorize the operation.

The operation becomes executable only when:

IDENTITY
+
AUTHENTICATION
+
PERMISSION
+
SCOPE
+
PRIVACY
+
SECURITY
+
GOVERNANCE

produce an authorized decision.

This prevents PRSL-AI from becoming an intelligence system with
unbounded access to the user's digital life.

The architecture instead creates a controlled model in which
intelligence can be powerful while authority remains explicitly
bounded.

